context_summaries = ""
i = 0
for d in context:
    i = i + 1
    prompt = "You are given a single document to analyze for a riddle-like identification of a political figure. Extract any possible matches to these clues, quoting the supporting lines and providing your reasoning:\n\nClues to check (answer Yes/No/Unknown for each, plus quotes and reasoning):\n1) First year in political office (for the principal role they are known for) was the same year as a FIFA World Cup.\n2) Last year in office was within three years of the release of an iconic film (e.g., Casablanca 1942; Gone with the Wind 1939; Citizen Kane 1941; The Godfather 1972; Jaws 1975; Star Wars 1977; Titanic 1997; The Matrix 1999; etc.). Identify such a film and the Δ years.\n3) They were reported to take a nap every day after lunch.\n4) They met with a U.S. Secretary of State; in one conversation, a phrase referring to a type of informal telegraph (e.g., “bush telegraph,” “jungle telegraph,” “grapevine telegraph”) was used.\n5) That meeting with the U.S. Secretary of State occurred within the last four years of their time in office.\n6) They held that office for less than 15 years total.\n7) They had three children (exactly three).\n8) A professional hunter paid them a compliment (quote/summary and source if present).\n9) They died on a Saturday (compute day-of-week if a death date is given and not stated).\n10) Identify any associated person whose first name matches a gin-cocktail name (examples: Tom [Tom Collins], Gibson, Gimlet, Negroni, Vesper, Aviation, Ramos, French [75], Bee [Bee’s Knees], Collins, etc.), and state that person’s relationship to the political figure.\n\nFor each potential figure found in this document, provide:\n- Name\n- Office held and years in office (start–end)\n- How each clue matches (with quotes and reasoning)\n- Any additional context that connects multiple clues\n\nDocument:\n---\n" + d + "\n---\nProvide a compact but thorough extraction for this single document only."
    extraction = llm_query(prompt)
    context_summaries = context_summaries + "\n\n[DOC " + str(i) + " EXTRACTION]\n" + extraction

final_prompt = "We have multiple document-level extractions about a political figure matching a set of clues. Your task: synthesize across the extractions to identify the single best match and answer the final query concisely.\n\nClues recap:\n- First year in office is the same year as a FIFA World Cup.\n- Last year in office is within three years of an iconic film’s release.\n- Reported to take a nap every day after lunch.\n- Met with a U.S. Secretary of State; in one conversation a phrase referring to an informal telegraph (e.g., “bush telegraph,” “jungle telegraph,” “grapevine telegraph”) was used.\n- That meeting occurred within the last four years of their time in office.\n- Held their office for less than 15 years.\n- Had three children.\n- A professional hunter paid them a compliment.\n- Died on a Saturday.\n- Request: Provide the name of this political figure, and the relationship this figure had with a person whose first name is the same as a cocktail typically made with gin (e.g., Tom for Tom Collins; Gibson; Gimlet; Negroni; Vesper; etc.). Provide the associated person’s full name and the relationship.\n\nHere are the document-based extractions:\n" + context_summaries + "\n\nNow, based on the above, do the following:\n1) Identify the political figure who fits all the clues (or best fits them if minor discrepancies exist in sources, but only if the overall fit is compelling and the document evidence supports it).\n2) Identify the person with the gin-cocktail first name, state their full name and specify clearly the relationship to the political figure (e.g., ‘mentor’, ‘spouse’, ‘parent’, ‘ally’, ‘assassinated by’, ‘foreign counterpart’, etc.).\n3) Keep the final output to one succinct line with this format: Name — Relationship to [Full Name of gin-cocktail-first-name person]: [relationship]."
result = llm_query(final_prompt)
return_result(result)